 is 1444. Then multiply by 100 to get 144400..\n\nNow I have three partial products: 2166 (from ones place), 25270 (from tens place), and 144400 (from hundreds place). I need to add them all together. Let's start by adding 2166 and 25270. .\n\n2166 + 25270. Let's break it down: 2000 + 25270 is 27270, then add 166 more. 27270 + 166 = 27436. .\n\nNow add 144400 to that. 144400 + 27436</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
