      "text": "64050 + 427000 = 491050.\n\nWait, no, that's not right. Wait, 4270 +59780 is 64050, then adding 427000 gives 64050 +427000 = 491050. But wait, 64050 +427000 is 491050? Let me check: 427000 +64050.\n\n427000 +64050:.\n\n427000 +60000 = 487000.\n487000 +4050 = 491050. Yes, correct.\n\nSo the final product is 491050.\n\nBut wait, let me verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the standard multiplication method.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n   854\n\u00d7 575\n--------\nFirst, multiply 854 by 5 (ones place): 4270.\nThen, multiply 854 by 70 (tens place): 59780.\nThen, multiply 854 by 500 (hundreds place): 427000.\nNow, add them all together: 4270 +59780 +427000 = 491050.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the product of 854 and 575 is 491,050.\n\n**Answer**\nThe product of 854 and 575 is \\boxed{491050}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 854 and 575, we break down the multiplication into three steps based on the place values of 575.\n\n1. **Multiply 854 by the ones place digit (5) of 575:**\n   \\[\n   854 \\times 5 = 4270\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 854 by the tens place digit (7) of 575, then add a zero:**\n   \\[\n   854 \\times 7 = 5978 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero to make it 59780)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 854 by the hundreds place digit (5) of 575, then add two zeros:**\n   \\[\n   854 \\times 5 = 4270 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros to make it 427000)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   4270 + 59780 + 427000 = 491050\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 854 and 575 is \\boxed{491050}.",
