      "text": "146,115.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 255 and 573 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into three parts based on the place values of 573:\n\n1. Multiply 255 by the ones place (3) of 573:  \n   \\( 255 \\times 3 = 765 \\)\n\n2. Multiply 255 by the tens place (70) of 573:  \n   \\( 255 \\times 70 = 17,\\!850 \\)\n\n3. Multiply 255 by the hundreds place (500) of 573:  \n   \\( 255 \\times 500 = 127,\\!500 \\)\n\nFinally, sum all the results:  \n\\( 765 + 17,\\!850 + 127,\\!500 = 146,\\!115 \\)\n\n**Answer:**  \n\\boxed{146115}",
