te 375 * 7 first. Wait, we already did 375 *7 earlier as part of the tens place calculation, which was 2625. So 2625 * 100 = 262,500. That's the third part..\n\nNow, adding all three parts together: 1875 (from ones place) + 26,250 (tens place) + 262,500 (hundreds place). Let's add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 1875 + 26,250. Let me add 1875 + 26,250. 26,250 + 1,000 is 27,250, plus 875 is 28,125. Wait, no. Let me do it correctly. 26,250 + 1,875. Breaking it down: 26,250 + 1,000 = 27,250; 27,250 + 800 = 28,050; 28,050 +75=28,125. So the sum of the first two is 28,125..\n\nNow add 262,500 to that. 262,500 + 28,125</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
