e right:.\n7 + 0 =7.\n6 +7=13, carry over 1.\n4 +6 +1=11, carry over 1.\n5 +4 +1=10.\n\nSo that's 60,137? Wait, maybe I did that wrong. Let's do it more carefully:.\n\n5467.\n+54670.\n= (5000 + 400 + 60 +7) + (50,000 + 4000 + 600 +70).\n= 50,000 + (5000 +4000) + (400 +600) + (60 +70) +7.\n=50,000 +9,000 +1,000 +130 +7.\n=50,000 +10,000 +130 +7.\n=60,000 +137.\n=60,137. Okay, that makes sense..\n\nNow add 60,137 to 156,200. Let's do that:.\n\n60,137 + 156,200. Break it down:.\n\n60,000 + 156,200 =216,200</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
