ternatively, I can think of 50 as 5 × 10, so 129 × 50 = (129 × 5) × 10 = 645 × 10 = 6450. That seems right. So the second part is 6450..\n\nNow, the hundreds place digit is 9, which represents 900. So I need to multiply 129 by 900. To do this, I can multiply 129 by 9 and then by 100. Let's calculate 129 × 9 first. 100 × 9 = 900, 20 × 9 = 180, 9 × 9 = 81. Adding those: 900 + 180 = 1080, plus 81 is 1161. Then multiply by 100 to get 1161 × 100 = 116100. So the third part is 116,100..\n\nNow, I have three components: 645 (from the ones place), 6450 (from the tens place), and 116,100 (from the hundreds place). I need to add all these together to get the final product. Let's add them step by step..\n\nFirst, add 645 and 6450. 645 + 6450. Let me add 645 + 6450. 6450 + 600 is 7050, then plus 45 is 7095. So that's 7095. Then add 7095 to 116,100. 7095 + 116,100</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
