, total 81+1350+2700=4131. So in that case, they didn't shift the positions but just multiplied by the actual place values. So similarly here, 816 is broken into 6, 10, 800. So each part is multiplied and summed..\n\nSo then, after 6 comes 10. So 851 ×10=8510. Then the hundreds place: 8 in the hundreds place is 800. So 851 ×800. Let me compute that. 851 ×800. Well, 851 ×8 is 6808, then add two zeros at the end, making it 680800. Wait, let me check that again. 800 is 8×100, so 851×8=6808, then times 100 is 680800. Yes. So that's 680800..\n\nNow, adding all three parts together: 5106 (from 6), 8510 (from 10), and 680800 (from 800). Let's sum these up step by step. First, 5106 + 8510. Let's add those. 5106 + 8510: 5000+8000=13000, 106+510=616, so total 13000 + 616 = 13616. Then add 680800 to that. 13616 + 680800</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
